---
/** Review-loop flowchart (CLAUDE.md §4). The decision diamond is the evaluated step. */
const steps = [
  'Formulate search',
  'Retrieve and prioritise',
  'Assess eligibility',
  'Extract findings',
  'Inspect synthesis',
];
const X = 60;
const W = 220;
const H = 44;
const STEP = 76;
const Y0 = 16;
const CX = X + W / 2;
const D = { cy: 452, hw: 120, hh: 52 };
const lastBottom = Y0 + (steps.length - 1) * STEP + H;
const term = { y: 548, w: 170, h: 44 };
---
<figure class="loop">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 400 606"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="loop-title loop-desc"
    focusable="false"
  >
    <title id="loop-title">The review loop</title>
    <desc id="loop-desc">
      A flowchart. Formulate search, then retrieve and prioritise, assess eligibility, extract findings and inspect
      the synthesis. A decision follows: gaps or contradictions, search again? If yes, the loop returns to
      formulate search. If no, the agent stops and submits. The decision is marked as the evaluated step.
    </desc>
    <defs>
      <marker id="loop-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" class="head" />
      </marker>
    </defs>

    {steps.map((label, i) => {
      const y = Y0 + i * STEP;
      return (
        <g>
          <rect class="box" x={X} y={y} width={W} height={H} rx="2" />
          <text class="label" x={CX} y={y + H / 2 + 5} text-anchor="middle">{label}</text>
          {i < steps.length - 1 && (
            <line class="edge" x1={CX} y1={y + H} x2={CX} y2={y + STEP - 2} marker-end="url(#loop-arrow)" />
          )}
        </g>
      );
    })}

    <line class="edge" x1={CX} y1={lastBottom} x2={CX} y2={D.cy - D.hh - 2} marker-end="url(#loop-arrow)" />

    <text class="eval-label" x={X - 10} y={D.cy - D.hh - 10}>Evaluated step</text>
    <path
      class="decision"
      d={`M ${CX - D.hw} ${D.cy} L ${CX} ${D.cy - D.hh} L ${CX + D.hw} ${D.cy} L ${CX} ${D.cy + D.hh} Z`}
    />
    <text class="label small" x={CX} y={D.cy - 5} text-anchor="middle">Gaps or contradictions?</text>
    <text class="label strong" x={CX} y={D.cy + 16} text-anchor="middle">Search again?</text>

    <path
      class="edge"
      d={`M ${CX + D.hw} ${D.cy} H 360 V ${Y0 + H / 2} H ${X + W + 2}`}
      marker-end="url(#loop-arrow)"
    />
    <text class="branch" x={CX + D.hw + 10} y={D.cy - 8}>Yes</text>

    <line class="edge" x1={CX} y1={D.cy + D.hh} x2={CX} y2={term.y - 2} marker-end="url(#loop-arrow)" />
    <text class="branch" x={CX + 10} y={D.cy + D.hh + 26}>No</text>

    <rect class="terminal" x={CX - term.w / 2} y={term.y} width={term.w} height={term.h} rx={term.h / 2} />
    <text class="label" x={CX} y={term.y + term.h / 2 + 5} text-anchor="middle">Stop and submit</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    <span class="fig-num">Figure 2</span>
    The review loop. An agent formulates a search, retrieves and prioritises records, assesses eligibility,
    extracts findings and inspects the emerging synthesis. If it sees gaps or contradictions it searches again;
    otherwise it stops and submits. The workshop evaluates that decision: whether to search again.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .loop {
    margin: var(--space-6) 0;
    max-width: var(--figure-max);
    padding: var(--space-5) var(--space-4) var(--space-4);
    background: var(--wash);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }

  svg {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 25rem;
    height: auto;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .box,
  .terminal {
    fill: var(--paper);
    stroke: var(--ink);
    stroke-width: 1.25;
  }

  .decision {
    fill: #fbf3e2;
    stroke: var(--pooled);
    stroke-width: 2.5;
  }

  .edge {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--ink);
    stroke-width: 1.25;
  }

  .head {
    fill: var(--ink);
  }

  .label {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 15px;
    fill: var(--ink);
  }

  .label.small {
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .label.strong {
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .branch {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    fill: var(--ink);
  }

  .eval-label {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 700;
    fill: var(--pooled-text);
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: var(--text-xsmall);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  .fig-num {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-right: 0.4em;
  }
</style>
